# start Validation Reply Form
_vrf_SHFSU01_shelx
;
PROBLEM: The absolute value of parameter shift to su ratio > 0.20
RESPONSE: parameter shift could not converge due to large amount of 
disorder present. equal but opposite orientations of atoms resulted in
oscillating values; however, the refined atomic positions still are
chemically reasonable.
;
_vrf_PLAT080_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Maximum Shift/Error ............................       1.90 Why ? 
RESPONSE: Issues with convergence occur due to the highly disordered 
nature of the organics. The equal but opposite cations in 50:50 mixture
results in oscillating paramters; nonetheless, the positions still refine
to chemically reasonable values.
;
_vrf_PLAT971_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.52A   From I2              4.56 eA-3  
RESPONSE: Slight excess density is present near the I2 position due to
the layered nature of the material, leading to stacking faults and thus
disorder in the inorganic layers.
;
_vrf_PLAT973_shelx
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Positive Resid. Density on       Pb1       3.80 eA-3  
RESPONSE: Similar to the issue with I2, the disordered nature of the 
compound, along with the layered nature, results in slight residual
electron density to be present.
;
# end Validation Reply Form
